# App

The whole frontend: what the page knows, what it does, and what it looks like.

`## Page /` says where it serves, and a page mounts itself. `State:` is what it
knows, `Actions:` is what it does, `View:` is real HTML with `{…}` holes, and
`Style:` is real CSS scoped to it. One click is one turn — the action runs, the
page paints once, and if the action fails the state goes back to what it was.

Nothing here parses a response by hand. `Get "/api/todos" as Seq of Todo` decodes
through the codec DERIVED from `## A Todo has:`, the same one the server encodes
with — so the two halves cannot drift.

Import Shared.

## Note
How many todos are still to do — a plain function, so the derived field below can
say what it means instead of counting inline.

## To countUndone (todos: Seq of Todo) -> Int:
    Let mutable n be 0.
    Repeat for t in todos:
        If t's done is equal to false:
            Set n to n + 1.
    Return n.

## Note
The glyph a row's tick button shows. A done todo is ticked; an open one is not.

## To tickMark (done: Bool) -> Text:
    If done:
        Return "[x]".
    Return "[ ]".

## Component TodoRow (todo: Todo) and (toggle: fn(Int) -> Unit) and (remove: fn(Int) -> Unit)

View:
    <li class:done={todo's done}>
      <button class="tick" on-click={toggle(todo's id)} aria-label="toggle {todo's text}">{tickMark(todo's done)}</button>
      <span class="text">{todo's text}</span>
      <button class="del" on-click={remove(todo's id)} aria-label="delete {todo's text}">delete</button>
    </li>

Style:
    li { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .6rem; padding: .45rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
    .text { flex: 1; }
    .done .text { text-decoration: line-through; opacity: .55; }
    .del { background: transparent; color: var(--danger); padding: .3rem .5rem; }

## Page /

State:
    Let todos be a new Seq of Todo.
    Let draft be "".
    Let error be "".
    Let left always be countUndone(todos).

Actions:
    When the page loads:
        Get "/api/todos" as Seq of Todo, then loaded.

    To loaded (answer: Result of Seq of Todo and HttpError):
        Inspect answer:
            When Ok (list):
                Set todos to list.
                Set error to "".
            When Err (e):
                Set error to e's message.

    To add:
        If draft is not equal to "":
            Post "text=" + urlEncode(draft) to "/api/todos" as Seq of Todo, then loaded.
            Set draft to "".

    To toggle (id: Int):
        Post "" to "/api/todos/toggle/{id}" as Seq of Todo, then loaded.

    To remove (id: Int):
        Post "" to "/api/todos/delete/{id}" as Seq of Todo, then loaded.

View:
    <main>
      <h1>Todos <small id="left">{left} left</small></h1>
      <form id="add" on-submit.prevent={add}>
        <input id="draft" type="text" placeholder="What needs doing?" bind={draft}>
        <button type="submit">Add</button>
      </form>
      {if error is not "":}<p class="error" role="alert">{error}</p>{end}
      <ul class="todos">
        {for each t in todos:}
          <TodoRow todo={t} toggle={toggle} remove={remove}/>
        {else:}
          <li class="empty">Nothing to do.</li>
        {end}
      </ul>
    </main>

Style:
    main { max-width: 34rem; margin: 3rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; }
    h1 { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: .6rem; }
    h1 small { font-size: .85rem; font-weight: 400; color: var(--muted); }
    form { display: flex; gap: .5rem; margin: 1rem 0; }
    input { flex: 1; }
    .error { color: var(--danger); font-weight: 600; }
    .todos { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
    .empty { color: var(--muted); padding: .45rem 0; }

## Test: a todo typed into the form is added

Given that POST "/api/todos" answers 200 with "[{{\"id\": 1, \"text\": \"milk\", \"done\": false}}]".
Type "milk" into "#draft".
Submit "#add".
Expect that the text of ".text" is equal to "milk".
Expect that the text of "#left" is equal to "1 left".
Expect that the value of "#draft" is equal to "".

## Test: a todo is ticked, then deleted

Given that POST "/api/todos" answers 200 with "[{{\"id\": 1, \"text\": \"milk\", \"done\": false}}]".
Given that POST "/api/todos/toggle/1" answers 200 with "[{{\"id\": 1, \"text\": \"milk\", \"done\": true}}]".
Given that POST "/api/todos/delete/1" answers 200 with "[]".
Type "milk" into "#draft".
Submit "#add".
Click ".tick".
Expect that the text of "#left" is equal to "0 left".
Expect that the count of "li.done" is equal to 1.
Click ".del".
Expect that the text of ".empty" is equal to "Nothing to do.".

## Test: an empty draft adds nothing

Submit "#add".
Expect that the text of ".empty" is equal to "Nothing to do.".
Expect that the text of "#left" is equal to "0 left".
